* DAT step 4b -- an above-the-line REAL frame.  The last hardware
* question on this route.
*
* Passed so far:
*   1  00600D   tables accepted, DAT runs
*   2  00600D   translation demonstrably walks our page table
*   3  006003   AMODE 31 entered and left, DAT still correct there
*   4a 006004   virtual 01005000, ABOVE the line, translated to real
*               frame 7 below it
*
* 4a settled the virtual side.  This moves the real frame above the line
* too:
*
*     virtual 01005000  ->  real 01100000        (17 MB)
*
* ORDER MATTERS HERE, differently from 4a.  With DAT off in 24-bit mode
* real 01100000 is not addressable at all -- it truncates.  So the
* checks run in 31-bit mode with DAT OFF, where addresses are real and
* bits 1-31 wide, and 31-bit mode is entered BEFORE the frames are
* cleared rather than after.  There is no return to 24-bit.
*
* There is a FOURTH check, and it earns its place: write 55 to real
* 01100000 and read it back in 31-bit real mode, before translation is
* involved at all.  If real storage above the line is simply not usable,
* that is a different and more basic failure than translation failing to
* reach it -- and without this check the two would give the same answer.
*
* Paste over hercules.rc.  Then EXIT HERCULES AND START IT AGAIN, or
* stop / sysclear / script hercules.rc .
*
* PASS IS 006005.

stop

r 0=0008000000002000

