* --- go ---------------------------------------------------------------
t+
restart

* Read the instruction address in the resulting PSW:
*
*   006005  PASS.  A virtual address above the 16 MB line translated to
*           a real frame above the line.  Both sides of the line work,
*           and the hardware question on this route is closed.
*
*   000BA8  Real storage above the line is not usable at all -- the 55
*           written in 31-bit real mode did not read back.  Nothing
*           about translation is implicated; check MAINSIZE first.
*
*   000BA6  Real storage above the line works, but the translated store
*           did not arrive there.
*
*   000BA7  Real 5000 was modified: the virtual address was truncated to
*           24 bits.
*
*   000B31  The switch to 31-bit did not take.
*
*   000DED  Program check.  Then  r 8E.2 :
*             0005  addressing exception -- the frame is outside
*                   MAINSIZE, so raise it
*             0010  segment translation, 0011 page translation,
*                   0012 translation specification
*
* Confirm which program ran:
*
*     X'2014' must disassemble as  L     3,178(0,15)
*     GR03 must read 01100000, GR06 must read 01005000
*     GR15 must read 00002002
*
* And by hand afterwards -- note these need 31-bit real addressing, so
* read them from the panel rather than from 24-bit code:
*
*     r 1100000.1   expect AA
*     r 5000.1      expect 00
